 ## Background
-3D Gaussian Splatting was introduced by Kerbl et al. in 2023 [S2][S6, unofficial]. It initializes positions using sparse point clouds from SfM tools like COLMAP [S2][S6, unofficial]. The method has since been extended to various domains including SLAM [S1], dynamic scenes [S1], and human avatars [S1]. It is implemented in various frameworks including IPOL demos [S2], OpenSplat [S3, unofficial], and Msplat [S4, unofficial].
+3D Gaussian Splatting was introduced by Kerbl et al. [9] (cited in [S1, S2]). It initializes positions using sparse point clouds from SfM tools like COLMAP [S2]. The method was developed to address the slow training and rendering speeds of NeRFs while maintaining high visual quality [S5, unofficial]. It has since been extended to various domains including SLAM [S1], dynamic scenes [S1], and human avatars [S1].
 
